# 222: functions and variables are SEPARATE namespaces (§6 `.42`) and there are
# no first-class functions (§1 non-goals), so a function name read as a value is
# an undefined VARIABLE — not an undefined function, and not some function-typed
# value. Note the two different messages in `error.rs` for the two namespaces:
# this is `undefined_name`, whereas case 221 is `undefined_function`.
--- source
fn f() { return 1; }
print f();
print f;
--- expect
1
error: Name at line 3: undefined variable 'f'
